  "purpose": {
    "thisIs": [
      "a historical attribution repair",
      "an owner evidence adjudication",
      "a per-slot decomposition of already-frozen Batch-01 evidence",
      "required so that the downstream A3 R17 slot-authority contract can mechanically bind acquisition authority for selection indices 0 and 2"
    ],
    "thisIsNot": [
      "a new acquisition",
      "a rerun",
      "a policy transition",
      "a replacement",
      "a methodology amendment",
      "a change to the Batch-01 execution record",
      "a change to the A3a pilot record",
      "an A3 run",
      "an A5 freeze authority"
    ],
    "whyOwnerAdjudicationIsRequired": "the public historical record omitted the slot -> opaque-run binding: the A3a pilot record deliberately carries no per-selection-index result (thisRecordCarriesNoPerSelectionIndexResult), and the only public occurrences of these two run references are unlabelled census lists (Option-B measurement-of-record compatibilityCensus.perRun, V4 transport-retry census runs), where reading a slot off an array position is forbidden",
    "whyThisIsNotMethodologyDiscretion": "the mapping is mechanically reconstructed from the frozen DRAW slot identity plus durable relational provenance in the database (fetch observations bound to the exact eche_row_key, organisation_id and root website claim); exactly one run satisfies it per slot, so nothing was chosen. SD9 is recomputed with the landed SD7 implementation and the existing frozen rule, unmodified."
  },
